# Simulator CLI and Outputs

## Two modes

```text
./simulator_207190406_209543255 -comparative simulation=<composition_yaml> \
    mission_control_folder=<folder> algorithm=<algorithm_so> [num_threads=<num>] [-verbose]

./simulator_207190406_209543255 -competition simulation=<composition_yaml> \
    mission_control=<mission_control_so> algorithms_folder=<folder> [num_threads=<num>] [-verbose]
```

| | Comparative | Competitive |
|---|---|---|
| Varies | every `MissionControl` `.so` in the folder | every algorithm `.so` in the folder |
| Fixed | one algorithm `.so` | one `MissionControl` `.so` |
| Output dir | `<mission_control_folder>/comparative_results_<time>` | `<algorithms_folder>/competition_<time>` |
| Report root key | `comparative_report` | `competitive_report` |
| Sort | by size of the agreeing group, **descending** | by `total_score` **desc**, then `total_steps` **asc** |

Both modes run **all configurations in the composition YAML** — the full (simulation, mission) pairs ×
drones × lidars expansion, per plugin.

## Argument parsing (graded behavior)

- Any order. `=` with **no** surrounding spaces. All arguments mandatory except `num_threads` and `-verbose`.
- Collect **all** problems before reporting; do not stop at the first.
- Unsupported arguments → usage + an error naming **every** unsupported argument → finish.
- Missing arguments → usage + an error naming **every** missing argument → finish.
- File argument pointing at a missing or unopenable file → usage + proper error → finish.
- Folder argument pointing at a missing/untraversable folder, **or a folder containing zero files of the
  expected kind** → usage + proper error → finish.
- "Finish" means return from `main` gracefully — never `exit()`.
- Usage text and error wording are our choice; make them specific enough to name the offending argument.

Parse and validate **before** loading anything or creating any output directory.

## Output directory

`<time>` must be freshly generated per run so an existing folder is never reused. A UTC timestamp with
seconds is fine, but must be checked for collision (two runs in the same second) — append a counter if
the directory already exists.

If the directory cannot be created, write a proper error to screen and finish.

Contents:

```text
<output_dir>/
  comparative_report.yaml            # or competitive_report.yaml - the single aggregate report
  <plugin>_simulation_output.yaml    # one ex2-style Simulation Result Output File per plugin
  <plugin>_run_NNNN_output_map.npy   # every output map, uniquely named and traceable to its run
  <plugin>_run_NNNN_error.log        # error log(s)
```

Exact file names are our choice, but **every output map must be traceable to the mission that produced
it** — encode the plugin name plus the run identity (simulation, mission, drone, lidar or the run index).
Document the chosen pattern in `README.md`.

## Report schemas

Field names and nesting come straight from the assignment doc — match them exactly.

```yaml
comparative_report:
  composition_file: "simulation_compositions.yaml"
  mission_control_folder: "folder"
  generated_at_utc: "2026-05-30T23:31:10Z"

  results_summary:            # sorted by number of agreeing managers, descending
    - same_results: ["manager1.so", "manager2.so", "manager5.so"]
      total_score: 495
      total_steps: 100
    - same_results: ["manager3.so"]
      total_score: 502
      total_steps: 124

  errors: ["manager7.so", "manager8.so"]   # could not be loaded / run
```

```yaml
competitive_report:
  composition_file: "simulation_compositions.yaml"
  mission_control: "mission_control_filename.so"
  generated_at_utc: "2026-05-30T23:31:10Z"

  results_summary:            # sorted by score descending, then steps ascending
    - algorithm: "algorithm1.so"
      total_score: 495
      total_steps: 100

  errors: ["algorithm2.so"]
```

- Plugin identifiers in the report are `.so` **filenames**, not paths.
- `errors` lists plugins that could not be loaded **or** run — they contribute no `results_summary` entry.
- `total_score` / `total_steps` are sums across all runs for that plugin; grouping in comparative mode is
  by the `(total_score, total_steps)` pair. Both are working assumptions — see `docs/open-questions.md`.
- Per-plugin `Simulation Result Output File` keeps the ex2 schema (see
  `../Drone-Mapper-ex2/readme.txt`, `simulation_output.yaml FORMAT`) with the plugin name added to the
  filename. `SimulationManagerReport` gained a `composition_file` field in ex3 — emit it.

## Inputs

Configs are YAML (`drone_config`, `mission_config`, `lidar_config`, `simulation_config`,
`simulation_compositions`); maps are `.npy`. `mission_config` YAML still uses the key `boundaries`, which
now populates `MissionConfigData::mission_bounds`. Mission boundaries are **local** coordinates — add
`simulation.map_axes_offset` when building the output map config (see `docs/map3d-contract.md`).

Report `resolution_request_status` per run as `ACCEPTED`, `IGNORED`, or `IGNORED TOO SMALL`.
